# VITE_API_BASE_URL is intentionally unset here. Leaving it unset lets the
# frontend fall back to `http://${window.location.hostname}:3000` (see
# API_BASE_URL in Login.tsx/DomainLogin.tsx/etc.), which works correctly
# whether this is opened via localhost or another machine's LAN IP — no
# hardcoded IP to go stale when DHCP hands out a different address.
#
# Previously hardcoded to a specific LAN IP (192.168.1.187) here, which had
# drifted from this machine's actual current IP (192.168.1.188) and was the
# root cause of a "Failed to fetch" on every login — the app was trying to
# reach a dead address regardless of which host the page was actually
# opened from.
#
# Only set this again if reviving tunnel-based testing (see
# docs/deployment/GCP-DEPLOYMENT.md's "Frontend -> backend wiring" section).
